Convert the following do…while loop to for loop:
int x=10;
do
{x--;
System.out.print(x);
}while (x>=1);

questions.solution:
int x;
for (x = 10; x >= 1; )
{
    x--;
    System.out.print(x);
}
(Both print 9876543210. Since x starts at 10, the condition is true on entry, so the for loop behaves exactly like the do-while.)

